- op: discuss  # 3a5c
  at: '2026-11-18T08:11:12Z'  # 3a5c
  by: agent  # 3a5c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3a5c
  clock: 4  # 3a5c
  nonce: 3a5c  # 3a5c
  message: "Merged in PR #2252 (dev a81dde10a..d7d39637d). The recorder wraps functools.lru_cache for repository code (not frozen modules, not installed packages): a body runs under its own coverage context |shared|cache|<file>::<qualname>, and every test that calls the cached function gets its rows at the fold. Reads and child processes of a body go to the callers of THAT cache entry (functools._make_key), not of the function: the first cut kept them per function and held 12,100 tests back from narrowing. Caches made before the recorder loaded are held back and named on the shared-work line.\nEvidence (fast_smart_test_build_11172026/caches/):\n- census_summary.txt: 24 cached functions in repository code; 26,352 misses in tests (~12 s); 14,816 tests had a hit on an entry another test filled, so they were never paired with the body.\n- logs/full2.log (smart-test --full on e4ac1c1ad): 41,330 passed, 12 skipped, 30 xfailed, 707.05 s, against 689-703 s in the three full runs without the cache step (inside run-to-run spread; one run each, not separable from noise). Fold: 66 fixture + 22 cache contexts, 41,372 tests given rows, 0 unused, 0 unwrapped. Never narrowed 427 (git-elsewhere 242, python 175, git 23).\n- live_control.txt (behavioral): _get_php_parser made to return None. The index pairs 16 tests of test_view_template_laravel.py with the function; in the campaign the 3 failing measured tests were NOT paired. 12 tests failed; the selector asked about that fault alone selected all 12, 0 neither selected nor named. The 3 campaign cases failed and were selected.\n- mutations.tsv: 35 planted, 34 red. Survivor E4 (except TypeError -> except KeyError around the per-entry lookup) is equivalent for a caller: the cache raises the same TypeError one line later.\n- prepr.sh (logs/prepr.txt): every gate rc=0; core 21,838 passed, root tests 2,895 passed.\nNot covered: hand-written caches and lazily filled module state (WI-supar); caches made before the recorder loads are held back from narrowing, not paired."  # 3a5c
